<Layout
  title="Claude Fable 5.2 - A.I. - Rycode"
  description="Claude Fable 5.2 is Anthropic’s model for hard, long-running technical work, available for general use, released 9 November 2026 at $8 input and $40 output per million tokens."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">Frontier models</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Claude Fable 5.2</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">Claude Fable 5.2 is Anthropic’s model for the hardest, longest-running technical work, available today on all platforms per <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/claude-fable-and-mythos-5-2">Introducing Claude Fable 5.2 and Claude Mythos 5.2</a> [1]. The <a href="https://assets.claude.com/27d60918d218125e7504bc7354c4b4626ec56b11.pdf">System Card</a> says it is “available for general use” [6]. It was released 9 November 2026 [1]. It upgrades <a href="/ai/models/anthropic/claude-fable-5-1/">Claude Fable 5.1</a> at a lower price of $8 input and $40 output per million tokens [1]. The API id is <code>claude-fable-5-2</code>, with a 1M-token context window and 128K max output, per the <a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/fable-5-2/overview">Fable 5.2 model page</a> [2]. Anthropic says Claude Fable and Claude Mythos are the same underlying model, and Fable has strong cybersecurity and biology safeguards so it can ship to all users [1]. For most coding and knowledge work Anthropic still recommends starting with <a href="/ai/models/anthropic/claude-opus-5-5/">Claude Opus 5.5</a>, then moving up to Fable or Mythos when Opus falls short [1]. The <a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/models/overview">models overview</a> says to use Claude Fable 5.2 for demanding reasoning and long-horizon agentic work [3].</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />
    <ModelFacts />
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Training</h2>
    <p>The Fable 5.2 model page lists a reliable knowledge cutoff of June 2026 and a training data cutoff of June 2026 [2]. Parameter count, training FLOPs, and the full post-training recipe are not in the sources on this page.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Inference</h2>
    <p>Adaptive thinking is always on and cannot be turned off. Default effort is <code>high</code> [2]. Anthropic says Fable 5.2 and Mythos 5.2 generate outputs up to 30% faster than Fable 5.1 and Mythos 5.1 [1]. An optional fast mode speeds up token generation by up to 2.5 times at $16 input and $80 output per million tokens [1]. Per the <a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing">pricing page</a>, fast mode is not available with the Batch API [4].</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Context</h2>
    <p>The documented context window is 1 million tokens. Max output is 128K tokens. Inputs are text and images. Output is text [2][3]. The pricing page says Claude 4.6 and later models (except Claude Haiku 5.5) include the full 1M token context window at standard pricing [4].</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Methods</h2>
    <p>Anthropic positions Fable 5.2 for demanding reasoning and long-horizon agentic work, and says it can act as Advisor or Orchestrator for smaller models [1][3]. Docs link a migration guide from Claude Fable 5.1 or from a Claude Opus model [2]. Claude Fable 5.1 was released 1 September 2026 and remains Active (legacy) per its <a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/fable-5-1/overview">model page</a> [9].</p>
    <p>Cybersecurity and biology classifiers block high-risk cyber activities and most tasks in research biology. When a query is blocked, users receive a response from Opus 4.8 for cybersecurity and Opus 5 for biology [1]. Anthropic reports about 55% fewer blocks than Fable 5.1 in early testing [1]. The model requires 30-day data retention and is not available under zero data retention unless Anthropic expressly authorizes it [2]. The System Card notes that Fable 5.2 falls back to Opus 4.8 more often than recent models in prompt injection scenarios [6].</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Benchmarking</h2>
    <p>Every score in the table below is Anthropic’s own, from the Fable 5.2 announce. None has been checked independently here. Anthropic says FrontierCode 2.0 at 49.1% (Xhigh) is the highest score of any released model it has tested [1].</p>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table ai-model-table--prose">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Eval</th>
            <th scope="col">Fable 5.2</th>
            <th scope="col">Fable 5.1</th>
            <th scope="col">Opus 5.5</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>FrontierCode 2.0 (Xhigh)</td><td>49.1%</td><td>32.4%</td><td>45.5%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>FrontierSWE v2</td><td>69.9%</td><td>56.3%</td><td>62.3%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Humanity&#x27;s Last Exam (with tools)</td><td>74.2%</td><td>65.6%</td><td>67.7%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>OSWorld 2.1 (offline set, partial)</td><td>89.3%</td><td>83.5%</td><td>87.2%</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Independent <a href="https://artificialanalysis.ai/models/claude-fable-5-2">Artificial Analysis</a> scores Claude Fable 5.2 (max, default fallback) at 65 on Intelligence Index v5.0.1, first on that board as of 9 November 2026 per the model page and the <a href="https://artificialanalysis.ai/leaderboards/models">LLM leaderboard</a> [7][8]. That Index score is not a lab announce score and is not a row in this site’s #aiBench table.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Access and pricing</h2>
    <p>Fable 5.2 is available for general use [6] and available today on all platforms named in the announce [1]. Docs status is Active (latest). Platforms: Claude API, Amazon Bedrock, Claude Models on Google Cloud (Google managed and Anthropic managed), Microsoft Foundry, and Claude Platform on AWS [2]. It is also in Claude apps on paid plans and seats that include Fable models [1]. Retirement is not sooner than 9 November 2027 per the model page and the <a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/model-deprecations">model deprecations</a> page [2][5].</p>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col"></th>
            <th scope="col">Fable 5.2</th>
            <th scope="col">Fable 5.1</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Input / MTok</td><td>$8</td><td>$10</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Output / MTok</td><td>$40</td><td>$50</td></tr>
          <tr><td>5m cache write / MTok</td><td>$10</td><td>$12.50</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1h cache write / MTok</td><td>$16</td><td>$20</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cache read / MTok</td><td>$0.20</td><td>$0.25</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Batch input / output / MTok</td><td>$4 / $20</td><td>$5 / $25</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Fast mode input / output / MTok</td><td>$16 / $80</td><td>Not offered</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Both input and output are 20% lower than Fable 5.1 on the pricing page ($10 to $8, $50 to $40) [4]. Fast mode is on the Claude API, Claude Code, Claude Models on Google Cloud (Anthropic managed and Google managed), and Microsoft Foundry (Anthropic hosted) [1]; on the Google managed option, Google sets its own price [4]. It is not available with the Batch API [4]. Bedrock and Google Cloud (Google managed) set their own prices and lifecycle dates [4][5]. US-only inference (<code>inference_geo: "us"</code>) adds a 1.1x multiplier on Claude 4.6 and later [4].</p>
